est result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\ntest result: ok. 23 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.88s\ntest result: ok. 15 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.23s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bumpkrfr7zodooxtkrfdttvewsz3u4jxhuvlhftucgihwtest2pa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte. No divergences found; `src/lib.rs` needed no fixes.**\n\nThe library is tiny (`int static_sum(int)` accumulating a function-scope `static int`, and `void driver(int)` printing 10 `printf(\"%d\\n\")` lines), so I did the work myself rather than delegating.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff | **empty** (`static_sum`, `driver`); 0 undefined non-libc syms |\n| Phase B — 21/21 `CONFIGS.md` rows | pass, seeded-random inputs per row |\n| Binary stdout | N/A (no `add_executable`/`[[bin]]`) — asserted, not assumed |\n| Phase C — 15/15 `ERRORS.md` rows | pass |\n| All feature combos | pass (no `[features]` → default + `--no-default-features`, × release *and* debug profiles) |\n\n## Two harness bugs I had to fix (either would have invalidated the result)\n\n1. **`cargo test` does not rebuild a `cdylib`** — integration tests never link it, so the suite was silently `dlopen`ing a **stale** `.so`. My first mutation run reported all six injected bugs as *passing*. Fixed with an `assert_not_stale()` guard (refuses to run against a `.so` older than `src/lib.rs`) plus an explicit build step in `check_all_features.sh`.\n2. **libtest progress text leaking into the `driver` stdout capture** — fd 1 is process-global, so parallel threads' `\"test foo ... ok\"` landed inside captured bytes and looked like a divergence. Fixed with a capture mutex, flushing Rust's `LineWriter` before stealing fd 1, `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1`, and an assertion that reports this as a *harness* error rather than a translation bug.\n\n## Anti-vacuity evidence\n\nSix deliberate bugs injected into `src/lib.rs`, each caught: `saturating_add` (10 failures), 9-iteration loop (9), `\"%d \"` format (9), `i+stride` (9), `#[no_mangle]` removed (14, incl. symbol parity), and a value-dependent off-by-one firing only at `update == 7` (3). `src/lib.rs` restored byte-identical afterwards.\n\n## Notes on design choices\n\n- `static_sum`'s hidden state means the *call sequence* is the input, so `Pair::fresh()` copies each `.so` to a unique temp path before `dlopen` — glibc then gives a distinct image with `sum` re-zeroed. Row 1 proves this holds.\n- `ERRORS.md` row 14 records honestly that null-pointer/length/out-of-range-enum boundaries are **structurally inapplicable** (both signatures are `int`-only, so all 2^32 bit patterns are valid); the test pins that against the header text so it fails loudly if the API ever grows a pointer or enum, and compensates with an exhaustive boundary-bit-pattern sweep.\n- Signed overflow is UB in C, so I rebuilt the ground truth at `-O0`, `-O2`, `-O3 -fstrict-overflow`, and `-Os` and re-ran everything: the Rust `wrapping_*` arithmetic matched at every level, so the match isn't an artifact of one codegen.\n\nFiles added under `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `check_all_features.sh`, `.cargo/config.toml`, `tests/{harness/mod.rs,differential.rs,error_paths.rs}`, plus the `libloading` dev-dependency. `c_src/` unmodified apart from the `build/` directory the task asked me to create.\n\nOne caveat: crates.io is unreachable from this sandbox, so cargo runs use `--offline` against the cached `libloading 0.8.9` (now pinned in `Cargo.lock`). `check_all_features.sh` takes `CARGO_FLAGS` if you want to drop that."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1198,"cache_read_input_tokens":87831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1198,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0de09701-f5af-4f1f-a137-e96ca83abd81","uuid":"88be009e-2dce-